n\n$(A_1,\\ldots,A_k)$ of $\\mathbb R^d$ satisfies\n\\[\n \\sum_{i=1}^k\\left\\|\\int_{A_i}x\\,d\\gamma_d(x)\\right\\|^2\n \\le\\frac9{8\\pi}.\n\\]\nEmpty cells are allowed. The constant is sharp whenever $d\\ge2$ and\n$k\\ge3$: three planar sectors of angle $2\\pi/3$, multiplied by the\northogonal complement of their plane, attain equality, with any further\ncells empty."},{"appendix":false,"contribution_target":{"fingerprint":"sha256:612bc83057c1feca623ec5ec98b335b6c82363ee26060165714f145986ae9b4c","grain":"paper-statement","id":"The-Gaussian-Propeller-Bound-in-Every-Dimension-September-24-2026#geo:constraints","title":"Constraints on the three largest radii"},"credit":{"kind":"producer-declared","license":null,"license_status":"consult-source-notice","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","repository":"https://github.com/openai/math","source":"lean/formalization.yaml","source_registry":"index.json#/sources"},"detail":{"path":"../rows/6aac54339df1dc016b8a19f0.json","pointer":"/row"},"display":"Corollary","id":"r:The-Gaussian-Propeller-Bound-in-Every-Dimension-September-24-2026:geo:constraints","manuscript_id":"p:The-Gaussian-Propeller-Bound-in-Every-Dimension-September-24-2026","name":"Constraints on the three largest radii","printed_number":"4.2","printed_number_provenance":{"atlas_pin":"f047bac96ee80ebef0b4f5a403831b84de6e32c1","binding":{"file":"build/sections/geometry.tex","label":"geo:constraints","line":137,"manuscript":"The-Gaussian-Propeller-Bound-in-Every-Dimension-September-24-2026","statement_sha256":"bc16baeb8a6539623e7b04994ed0050f36396acf1a378d549e809dd67211e2d1"},"blob_sha256":"sha256:253ae0683558fd095a71d6f47ab0694d8d98b846c1a65d2bbf9b145d484af567","kind":"reading-page-computed","pdf_verified":false,"pin":"f047bac96ee80ebef0b4f5a403831b84de6e32c1","renderer":"scripts/build_papers.py","source":"data/statement_numbers.json","upstream_pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb"},"printed_number_status":"recorded","reading_page":"papers/T